# The bare domain, dijonkitchen.org, deployed on its own to Netlify.
# The site itself is www.dijonkitchen.org on GitHub Pages.
# ADR 2026-11-07-fediverse-handle-on-own-domain says why.
# Netlify reads the first rule that matches and forwards query strings.

# Fediverse lookups for @dijonkitchen.org@dijonkitchen.org go to Bridgy Fed,
# as https://fed.brid.gy/docs#fediverse-enhanced asks.
/.well-known/host-meta*  https://fed.brid.gy/.well-known/host-meta:splat  302
/.well-known/webfinger*  https://fed.brid.gy/.well-known/webfinger  302

# Everything else goes to the canonical host, as Pages did before.
/*  https://www.dijonkitchen.org/:splat  301!
